        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "the symmetry of the Stanza. And hence the other reading would",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "be better as meaning “ where there is high sense of one’s own",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "greatness there is danger of misery.” This Stanza occurs at p.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "6 of the Kâvyasangraha.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXVI.—तुलितबिसिनीपत्रपयसाम् = which are like the water on",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the lotus-leaf, a very common simile.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXVII.—भ्रातः = comp. Nîtis'ataka St. 34. राजपरिषत् is scarce-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ly a good reading after we have already had सामन्तचक्रम्. It might,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "however, be taken as “that great assembly” “that high assembly.”",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Râmarshi renders it by विद्वद्गणधनाढ्यजनाद्युपलक्षिताः (sic) राजसभा. उद्रिक्तः =",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "क्रीडावशेन उच्छृङ्खलः उत्कटो वा (Râmarshi). कथाः = शृङ्गारवीरकरुणाद्भुतहास्यभया-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "नकाः (sic) बीभत्सरौद्रादिरसैरुत्कटेरमणीयत्वेनातिप्रसिद्धाः कथाः कथानकानि तत्र सभायां-",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "क्रियमाणा वार्ताः. स्मृतिपथ compare the next stanza and the English",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "expression “matter of history.”.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXVIII.—गमिताः = कालेनेति शेषः says Râmarshi. But there",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "is no mention of काल here except in the heading of this",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "section पुनः कालमुद्दिश्याह I think it must be taken as an instance of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the स्वार्थे णिच् see Raghu III., 50. For सिकतिल comp. Prasannarâghava",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "(Act. V.,) p. 171 and see Pâṇini V., 2, 104-5.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXIX.—रजनिदिवसौ—for the gender see Siddh. Kaum. I., 390,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "कालः = वर्तमानादिः क्षणादिसमयो वा Râmarshi. But neither seems to be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "very appropriate here. He also explains काली as स्वशक्ति i. e. Kâla’s",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "शक्ति. The other commentator renders the two respectively by मृत्यु",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "and कालरात्रि, for the latter of which I know of no authority",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "The two words seem to me here to signify the male",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "and female personifications of the Destructive Principle. Now काल",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "is given by the Medinîkâra as a name of Mahâkâla or Mahâdeva.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "काली is well known to be a name of Pârvatî, Mahâdeva is the Deity",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "of Destruction, and is also represented in the Purâṇas as playing",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "with Pârvatî. काल and काली therefore may here be taken to mean",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
